  "description": "Florida's 28th Congressional District covers all of Monroe County (the Florida Keys) and southwestern Miami-Dade County, including Homestead and the Hammocks. Incumbent Republican Rep. Carlos Gim\u00e9nez, first elected in 2020 after ousting Democrat Debbie Mucarsel-Powell, is seeking a fourth term. The district has a Cook Partisan Voting Index of R+10 and a heavily Hispanic population (72.7%). Democrats are holding a competitive primary between retired Navy Commander Phil Ehr and former Google executive Hector Mujica, with independent Eddy Rojas also on the general election ballot. A new congressional map passed in April 2026 may reshape the district's boundaries and political dynamics.",
